\begin_layout Standard
The approach starts from the point of view of a developer who has dealt
 with a problem (e.g.
 Mountain Car) in detail and has already written a program to solve it.
 Although the program is already very mature, there is a parallel RL solution
 that performs better than the expert's program.
 This solution is considered a black box and can thus not be explained.
 The Expert's program is now to be modified with genetic programming in
 such a way that it performs just as well as the black box, but still remains
 close enough to the expert program to allow the developer to recognize
 the necessary changes.
