\begin_layout Itemize
Reverse early: To reach the goal, you don't have to take the maximum momentum.
 If you turn back earlier, a lot of time can be saved.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Discard Action 1 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Do nothing
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

: Doing nothing makes no sense in principle - speed is lost when taking
 a swing and when turning around, instead of doing nothing two consecutive
 times, you could normally accelerate in the opposite direction.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Minimum number of necessary turns.
 Depending on the starting position, the goal can be reached deterministically
 with two turns (to the left, to the right) or with three turns (to the
 right, to the left, to the right).
 Since this decision is relatively far from the end, it is difficult to
 be learn by an agent.
\begin_inset Note Comment
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Mindestanzahl der erforderlichen Umdrehungen.
